From 42bb8d660d5bc21520b1964adfbd171330b0ce14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 23:15:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] inline-3d(#73): map the weave source through the quad's UVs,
 not the whole image

A tile clipped at the top of the viewport smears a "tail" below the element:
the clipped-off top reappears at the bottom as a constant-width column.

Measured on hardware with a runtime-side dump of the weave input, the SBS
atlas and the woven output (one file trigger, three PNGs). The artifact is
already present in the INPUT the browser packs, so nothing downstream is at
fault: the runtime's per-rect blits are vertically identity, the assembled
atlas is clean, and the DP weave is faithful.

Row-width profile of the left SBS half, element clipped 190px at the top:

    band row   content width
    0 .. 424   69..103, varying     <- the cube
    432..608   61, CONSTANT         <- one source row replicated downward

Constant width over 176 rows is texture edge-clamp: the computed source rect
over-reaches the bottom of the source image and Skia repeats the last row.
The replicated row still holds cube pixels, which is the only reason it is
visible -- had the source covered the whole element, its last row would be
the empty area below the cube and nothing would show. Scrolled far up the
source runs out entirely and the over-reach yields transparency instead, so
the artifact lives in a band of clip amounts rather than at the extreme,
which is exactly how it presents.

Cause: attempt_submit sub-regioned a clipped tile as a fraction of the WHOLE
resource image, i.e. assuming the quad draws its resource with UVs
(0,0)-(1,1). SurfaceAggregator recorded only quad->rect and dropped the UVs,
so that assumption was never checked. Record uv_top_left/uv_bottom_right (and
the quad's visible_rect) alongside the rect, and compose the clip fraction
with the UV window so the sub-region stays inside the pixels the resource
actually carries. With identity UVs the expression is unchanged, so the
unclipped and non-texture paths keep their current behaviour.

Also adds a throttled [DXR73] probe logging rect / quad_rect / quad_visible /
uv / image dims / computed src, flagging src.bottom past the image edge, so
the over-reach is visible in a log rather than only in pixels.
---
